## 19. NON-BLOCKING DESIGN

Avoid large `delay()` calls.

Use `millis()`-based scheduling.

Main loop should remain responsive.

Tasks include:

```text
HTTP server handling
node timeout checks
sensor collection cycles
STA reconnect
backend sync
storage cleanup
time sync
```

Suggested structure:

```cpp
void loop() {
    apiServer.handleClient();

    wifiManager.update();
    nodeRegistry.update();
    collectionManager.update();
    backendSyncManager.update();
    timeManager.update();
}
```

The exact API may differ.

Do not implement unnecessary FreeRTOS complexity unless there is a real reason.

Prefer a clean cooperative scheduler for the first prototype.

---

## 20. MEMORY AND RELIABILITY

Requirements:

- Use bounded JSON document sizes.
- Do not parse an unlimited body.
- Batch sensor records.
- Avoid excessive String copying.
- Avoid giant in-memory arrays.
- Close HTTP connections correctly.
- Check filesystem operation results.
- Check JSON deserialize errors.
- Check HTTP response codes.
- Use connection/request timeouts.
- One failed sensor node must not crash the gateway.
- Backend outage must not crash the gateway.

