Provide ONE of these approaches:

### Preferred

Create a small mock sensor-node script for a laptop using Python.

It should simulate:

```text
registration
GET /api/node/info
GET /api/node/data
POST /api/node/ack
```

However, because a laptop normally connects as a client to the ESP32 AP and cannot automatically behave exactly like an ESP8266 without configuration, explain how to run it and configure its IP/port.

OR:

Provide a compile-time:

```cpp
MOCK_NODE_MODE
```

that inserts one fake node into the registry and generates mock HTTP responses internally for testing CollectionManager.

Keep mock code isolated from production logic.

