## 24. IMPLEMENTATION PHASES

Implement in this exact order.

### PHASE 1 - Project bootstrap

- Create PlatformIO project.
- Configure ESP32 board.
- Serial logging.
- Mount LittleFS.

Expected Serial:

```text
[GATEWAY] Boot
[GATEWAY] LittleFS mounted
```

### PHASE 2 - Wi-Fi AP

- Start ESP32 AP.
- Print AP IP.

Expected:

```text
[GATEWAY] AP started
[GATEWAY] SSID=UAV_GATEWAY
[GATEWAY] IP=192.168.4.1
```

### PHASE 3 - Gateway API

Implement:

```text
GET /api/gateway/status
POST /api/gateway/nodes/register
GET /api/gateway/nodes
GET /api/gateway/time
```

Test using laptop/curl/Postman connected to ESP32 AP.

### PHASE 4 - Node registry/authentication

- Register node.
- Authenticate node.
- Track lastSeen.
- Mark stale node offline.

### PHASE 5 - Storage

- Save fake GatewayMeasurement.
- Reboot ESP32.
- Verify record remains.
- Verify duplicate prevention.

### PHASE 6 - Collection

- Use mock node or actual ESP8266 later.
- Request info.
- Request data.
- Save records.
- ACK stored records.

### PHASE 7 - Internet STA

- Add hotspot connection.
- Keep AP alive while STA reconnects.

### PHASE 8 - Backend sync

- Upload pending batches.
- Mark successful records.
- Preserve records when backend is unavailable.

Do NOT implement all phases as one uncontrolled code dump without validating dependencies.

